{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An adventure counts moves. A mystery counts minutes: every alibi in the house"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is stated as a time, and a player who cannot check one against a clock is being"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asked to take the game’s word for it. This library gives the move counter an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hour and a minute, a "},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" verb that reads it back, alarms that go off at a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"stated hour, and timetables that keep an actor where his day says he is."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The clock is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"derived, not ticked"}]},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock\/now","type":"reference"},{"text":" is a pure function of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"engine’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"moves","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so every rule, action, fuse and daemon in one turn reads the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same time, the timer tick that closes the turn included. A clock advanced by a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"daemon of its own would be read differently by daemons sorting before and after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, which would make the hour depend on other timers’ names. Deriving also","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inherits the engine’s own notion of world time: the hour doesn’t move on a parse","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"error or a meta command, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take all"},{"type":"text","text":" costs one turn rather than four."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"},{"text":" bundle rather than a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GamePlugin"},{"text":", because it has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state to keep — the minutes a game has moved the clock by hand, whether it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paused, and which stop each scheduled actor was last seen keeping. A bundle’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"globals namespace themselves and travel in save files, so the host lists the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"clock in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"content"},{"text":" and gets all three for nothing. Everything else belongs to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the host: the rooms, the actors, the bodies of the alarms, and the timetables. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Timetable","isActive":true},{"text":" holds no state of its own, which is what lets a game declare one","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as an ordinary computed property naming its own rooms, and what makes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Timetable\/location(at:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" an answer available at bootstrap, in a rule, and in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a plain unit test.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Gnusto","import GnustoClock          \/\/ .product(name: \"GnustoClock\", package: \"Gnusto\")","","struct Fulminate: Game {","    let clock = Clock(startingAt: TimeOfDay(17, 30), minutesPerTurn: 2, text: clockText)","","    static let clockText: Clock.Text = {","        var text = Clock.Text()","        text.timeIs = .naming { \"Your watch says \\($0).\" }","        return text","    }()","","    var content: GameContents { clock }        \/\/ the verb, the action, the saved state","","    var timers: [TimedEvent] {","        clock.schedule(teague, named: \"teague.day\", teagueDay)","","        clock.at(TimeOfDay(17, 46), named: \"clock.blast\") {","            blastHappened = true","        }","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reading the time needs a live turn, so ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock\/now","type":"reference"},{"text":" belongs in a rule body, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"describe","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block, an action or a timer, and not in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"evaluated at bootstrap. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block that wants to place a scheduled actor asks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the timetable instead, which reads no world state:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"teague.starts(in: teagueDay.location(at: clock.start))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A stored clock also","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hands the play-test status footer a ","type":"text"},{"code":"time=5:46 pm","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" field, which a timed game"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wants, since a line true at half past five and false at six reads the same in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"transcript that never says which it was.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"collection","title":"GnustoClock","modules":[{"name":"GnustoClock"}],"externalID":"GnustoClock","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustoclock"]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"The clock","anchor":"The-clock","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock","doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock\/Text"]},{"title":"Times of day","anchor":"Times-of-day","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeOfDay","doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeFormat"]},{"title":"An actor’s day","anchor":"An-actors-day","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Timetable","doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Stop"]},{"title":"Extended Modules","generated":true,"anchor":"Extended-Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Gnusto"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Puts a wall clock over the engine’s turn counter, so a game can be played"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"against an evening rather than a move count."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Clock/Text":{"title":"Clock.Text","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Text","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The clock’s own voice: the one line the mechanics print. Override the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"line at init to re-skin; the clock stores its table as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"let"},{"type":"text","text":", so init"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"is the only chance.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Text","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/clock\/text","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock\/Text"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Timetable":{"title":"Timetable","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Timetable"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An actor’s day, written down: a list of stops the clock walks them through.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Timetable"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/timetable","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Timetable"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Timetable/location(at:)":{"title":"location(at:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"location"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"at"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11GnustoClock9TimeOfDayV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TimeOfDay"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8LocationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Location"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Timetable\/location(at:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the actor is — or was, or will be — at a given time."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/timetable\/location(at:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/TimeOfDay":{"title":"TimeOfDay","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimeOfDay","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A time on a 24-hour wall clock, with no date attached: 8:15 in the evening"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeOfDay(20, 15)"},{"type":"text","text":", and it is the same value tomorrow."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TimeOfDay","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/timeofday","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeOfDay"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Clock/now":{"type":"topic","title":"now","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"now"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11GnustoClock9TimeOfDayV","text":"TimeOfDay"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock\/now","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What time it is now."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/clock\/now","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock","title":"GnustoClock","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Puts a wall clock over the engine’s turn counter, so a game can be played"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"against an evening rather than a move count."}]},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/TimeFormat":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeFormat","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimeFormat","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/timeformat","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/TimeOfDay"},{"type":"text","text":" is spelled for the player."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TimeFormat","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"TimeFormat"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Clock":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Clock","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Clock"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/clock","abstract":[{"text":"A wall clock over the turn counter: a game where it is twenty to six, and","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"ten to six four turns later.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Clock","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Clock"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Gnusto":{"type":"topic","title":"Gnusto","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Gnusto","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/gnusto","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoClock/documentation/GnustoClock/Stop":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One appointment on an actor’s day: where they are meant to be, from when."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Stop"}],"title":"Stop","url":"\/documentation\/gnustoclock\/stop","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoClock\/documentation\/GnustoClock\/Stop","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Stop"}]}}}